    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progress Toward Outcome: The revenue administration and project management support consulting firm were hired on 24 March 2022, and the contract was awarded for the Supply, Installation, Commissioning, and Maintenance of the Tax Administration Information System (TAIS) on 22 July 2022. Phase 1 of the TAIS upgrade is complete. The upgraded TAIS went live in August 2024 and is being used by the Inland Revenue Division. Refinements are still being made to ensure it meets IRD&apos;s requirements. Phase 2, ensuring the upgraded TAIS is interconnected with the Ministry of Finance and Treasury&apos;s other IT systems, will begin in 2025.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Audited Project Financial Statements | Mar 2025: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/53305/53305-001-apfs-en_0.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: Output 1a.Structure approved. Recruitment has commenced, and the reassignment of existing staff was completed in the first week of Q2 2024. Recruitment will occur over the next two years.b.Business process advisor has assisted in numerous meetings and brainstorming sessions on business processes, covering a range of topics, including registration, debt collection, non-filing enforcement, as well as components of processes (e.g., issuing garnishee notices to collect debts, imposing penalties at the end of an audit). A small debt reduction forum to discuss debt reduction strategies and processes was also formed, and represented by the Commissioner, both Deputy Commissioners, two Assistant Deputy Commissioners, a team leader, and four project advisers. Of the 10 members, one is a woman (10%).c.A management development program (targeting team leaders and above) was developed in 2024, and roll-out commenced in March 2025. Training on Governance has been undertaken for senior staff. All IRD senior female staff from Team Leader and above will be required to participate in this.d.This work will be guided and assisted by the IRD GAP. Based on discussions with central agency partners, there is no stand-alone training on gender equality, however elements are included in the &apos;Knowing Your Public Service course which is mandatory for onboarding and induction and also required for promotions and offered only twice a year. An introduction to gender equality induction has been developed and delivered to IRD Champions, another workshop developed and delivered to IRD Executive Team, and a series of GE info sessions were delivered to team leaders and employees. To date 104 of 130 employees. (80% of staff) have participated at these information sessions) 46 (or 44%) were men and 58 (or 56%) were women. Additional information sessions will be held in the new year to ensure that all staff receive the information.e.Work has not yet begun. GESI advisor to develop a tool that can be used to assess the gender impacts of IRD policies and programs, based on similar tools used by other tax administrations.Output 2a.Phase 1 of system upgrade has gone live as of 22 July 2024. Enhancements to the Business Intelligence database will be implemented as part of Phase 2. This will enable more flexible reporting. Sex-disaggregated data has been built into the system. Agreement on the scope of Phase 2, including the above, was signed off by both parties on 3 April 2025.b.Phase 1 of system upgrade has gone live as of 22 July 2024. This includes all tax administration core functionalities such as registration, cashing, assessment, audit, collection, objection and refunds. Some issues are still being identified and are progressively being fixed. Development/configuration of VAT is incomplete, but the tax will be applicable only in January 2026 at the earliest. Phase 2, which mainly covers external interfaces and business intelligence capabilities, has now been scoped. Agreement on the scope of Phase 2, was signed off by both parties on 3 April 2025. The system should be fully operational by the end of May 2026 almost 9 months behind schedule.. External interfaces with third parties will not occur in the way intended. A manual process will be developed.c.Training of end-users started in June 2024 and will continue on an ongoing basis until the conclusion of the project. Additional training maybe necessary with specific end-users and system administrators following Phase 2.Output 3a.Survey results reported in the third Quarter of 2023 will be used to inform the taxpayer services improvement plan. This was drafted in Q1 of 2024 and is now awaiting input and approval by IRD Management. In addition, following the endline survey, an assessment will be conducted to assess whether there has been an increase in satisfaction levels with IRD services (overall and by gender).b.Development of a taxpayer service and education strategy, incorporating LTO, was delayed due to other priorities in the debt management area. This was drafted in Q1 of 2024 and is now awaiting input and approval by IRD Management.c.When education/information sessions are delivered, we will pose a question to taxpayers to assess whether their knowledge/skills increased, with results to be disaggregated by gender.d.While VAT Bill was sent to Parliament before the 2024 General Election it was required to be reconsidered and resubmitted to Parliament. The Bill will be considered in the next few months. A more realistic start date for VAT is being proposed i.e. 1 January 2026.e.This work will be guided and assisted by the taxpayer service and education improvement strategies, with gender considerations applied. Preliminary information sessions have begun, with the VAT advisor providing information on how to calculate the transitional VAT input tax credit on the first VAT return during an information session to Chamber of Commerce and Industry on September 23, 2024.f.This work will be guided and assisted by the taxpayer service and education improvement strategies, with gender considerations applied.</narrative>
    </title>
